URE\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CHARTER:1-64+CULTURE:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"972dca61657b5271277e7a63647e4420761591b9d38425ccc3dba3a0dee430e9\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8269}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CHARTER_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6cb6875c0d4316fa8be25f0b568bd2924e571af7f2cb30e755336344339e5174\",\"source_size_bytes\":3964,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Restart authority and accountable disposition\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident lead may isolate equipment and order emergency stabilization. Only the independent quality unit may release a manufactured lot, and only the site head may authorize commercial restart after current quality, aseptic, utility, and cyber evidence is reconciled.\nEmergency procurement does not waive validated methods, operator qualification, chain of custody, environmental permits, data-integrity controls, or deviation review. A successful mechanical check is not lot release or commercial restart authority.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving lead acknowledges the same batch genealogy, fill-line configuration, cold-chain map, utility state, and control-system version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nASSAY and STERILE provide release evidence but cannot authorize release; REVIEW provides independent readiness findings but cannot execute restart.\nCHANGE binds candidate lineage while CHARTER preserves separation among stabilization, execution, verification, release, restart authorization, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-lead | v3 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | quality-unit | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | site-head | v3 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | regulatory-liaison | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-lead | v3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | quality-unit | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | site-head | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | regulatory-liaison | v3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-lead | v3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | quality-unit | v3 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | site-head | v3 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | regulatory-liaison | v3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-lead | v4 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | quality-unit | v4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | site-head | v4 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-015 | regulatory-liaison | v4 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-016 | incident-lead | v4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-017 | quality-unit | v4 | 3.8 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-018 | site-head | v4 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-019 | regulatory-liaison | v4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-020 | incident-lead | v4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-021 | quality-unit | v4 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-022 | site-head | v4 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-023 | regulatory-liaison | v4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-024 | incident-lead | v5 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-025 | quality-unit | v5 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-026 | site-head | v5 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-027 | regulatory-liaison | v5 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-028 | incident-lead | v5 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-029 | quality-unit | v5 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-030 | site-head | v5 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-031 | regulatory-liaison | v5 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-032 | incident-lead | v5 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-033 | quality-unit | v5 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-034 | site-head | v5 | 3.7 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-035 | regulatory-liaison | v5 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-036 | incident-lead | v6 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-037 | quality-unit | v6 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-038 | site-head | v6 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-039 | regulatory-liaison | v6 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-040 | incident-lead | v6 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-041 | quality-unit | v6 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nName who may isolate, repair, verify, release a lot, restart operations, and close.\nTreat semantic records and candidate mutations as non-authoritative work products.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CULTURE_PROCESS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4afe715ed5a632f384658d45a19fda0c6f1bc5476bc24ab525c75687df9c5d46\",\"source_size_bytes\":3843,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Bioreactor state, yield, and hold-time evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current engineering batch achieved 72 percent yield. The restart gate is at least 68 percent yield in two consecutive engineering batches; one 72 percent batch is insufficient.\nHarvest hold time is limited to six hours at 2 to 8 degrees Celsius. Six hours is not the downstream twelve-hour formulated-bulk limit.\nA media lot, inoculum, control recipe, reactor sensor, transfer path, or hold vessel change makes earlier process evidence stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nASSAY disposition consumes CULTURE genealogy and results; CURRENT utilities and SIGNAL observations constrain whether CULTURE evidence remains applicable.\nCHANGE records every recipe and equipment mutation; REVIEW requires current candidate-bound evidence for both consecutive batches.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| BIO-000 | reactor-a | v3 | 72.0 | percent-yield | superseded |\n| BIO-001 | reactor-b | v3 | 73.7 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-002 | harvest-tank | v3 | 72.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-003 | transfer-loop | v3 | 74.2 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-004 | reactor-a | v3 | 73.0 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-005 | reactor-b | v3 | 74.7 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-006 | harvest-tank | v3 | 73.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-007 | transfer-loop | v3 | 72.3 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-008 | reactor-a | v3 | 74.0 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-009 | reactor-b | v3 | 72.8 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-010 | harvest-tank | v3 | 74.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-011 | transfer-loop | v3 | 73.3 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-012 | reactor-a | v4 | 72.1 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-013 | reactor-b | v4 | 73.8 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-014 | harvest-tank | v4 | 72.6 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-015 | transfer-loop | v4 | 74.3 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-016 | reactor-a | v4 | 73.1 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-017 | reactor-b | v4 | 74.8 | percent-yield | superseded |\n| BIO-018 | harvest-tank | v4 | 73.6 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-019 | transfer-loop | v4 | 72.4 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-020 | reactor-a | v4 | 74.1 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-021 | reactor-b | v4 | 72.9 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-022 | harvest-tank | v4 | 74.6 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-023 | transfer-loop | v4 | 73.4 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-024 | reactor-a | v5 | 72.2 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-025 | reactor-b | v5 | 73.9 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-026 | harvest-tank | v5 | 72.7 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-027 | transfer-loop | v5 | 74.4 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-028 | reactor-a | v5 | 73.2 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-029 | reactor-b | v5 | 72.0 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-030 | harvest-tank | v5 | 73.7 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-031 | transfer-loop | v5 | 72.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-032 | reactor-a | v5 | 74.2 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-033 | reactor-b | v5 | 73.0 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-034 | harvest-tank | v5 | 74.7 | percent-yield | superseded |\n| BIO-035 | transfer-loop | v5 | 73.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-036 | reactor-a | v6 | 72.3 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-037 | reactor-b | v6 | 74.0 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-038 | harvest-tank | v6 | 72.8 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-039 | transfer-loop | v6 | 74.5 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-040 | reactor-a | v6 | 73.3 | percent-yield | current |\n| BIO-041 | reactor-b | v6 | 72.1 | percent-yield | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve yield, consecutive-batch count, temperature, hold time, and candidate currency.\nDistinguish process performance from lot release and commercial restart.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
